      "anchorExample": "A single flu virion (Orthomyxovirus): helical capsid, enveloped, RNA — traced through every lesson to show how classification traits describe a real virus.",
      "courseTitle": "Viruses: Structure, Classification & What It Means to Be Alive",
      "courseGoal": "Students can describe what a virus is, explain why viruses depend on a host cell, identify the parts of a virus, and classify any virus using capsid shape, envelope, and nucleic acid type.",
      "nodes": [
